+# Media credits
+
+- `coffee-pour.mp4`: [Pouring coffee in a cup](https://mixkit.co/free-stock-video/pouring-coffee-in-a-cup-43941/), Mixkit, 720p stock clip.
+- `coffee-roaster.mp4`: [Coffee roaster in operation](https://mixkit.co/free-stock-video/coffee-roaster-in-operation-88001/), Mixkit, 720p stock clip.
+- Both videos are provided under the [Mixkit Stock Video Free License](https://mixkit.co/license/#videoFree). They have no audio track. The JPEG posters are frames extracted from their respective clips.
+- The remote podcast is [Home Coffee Roasting, part 1](https://hackerpublicradio.org/eps/hpr3563/index.html), by dnt for Hacker Public Radio, episode 3563 (March 30, 2022). Unmodified audio, [CC BY-SA 4.0](https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/). The page links to the original transcript and episode notes.
+
+The hero is intentionally eager with metadata preloading and no autoplay. Below-the-fold media use native lazy loading where supported. Other browsers receive media and poster URLs only within 200px of the viewport. Keep those URLs in `data-src` and `data-poster` in the HTML; setting real `src` or `poster` attributes there would allow the preload scanner to start requests before the fallback runs. No-script visitors get explicit links rather than eager downloads.
